v1.13
  /Dc/0/Temperature now carries the hotter of the two MOSFETs instead of MOSFET 2
  alone - the device page, the alarm and the ReadMe now refer to the same number
  ReadMe (de/en): new section on naming in Node-RED. The Victron nodes label
  /Dc/0/Temperature "Battery temperature 0" and /Dc/1/Voltage "Battery voltage 1"
  from their own fixed list; the section names the correctly labelled paths to
  use instead (/Dc/In/V, and the separate temperature devices)

v1.12
  everything in the package is English now: log messages, comments in the driver,
  and the node names, comments and status texts of the Node-RED flow in extras/
  the flow reports failures instead of always claiming success - the status text
  now comes from the exec return code, not from both outputs at once
  the Node-RED flow and its description are part of the repository and the ReadMe
  (de/en); no functional change to the driver itself

v1.11
  first version that is complete and stable in daily use. It publishes every
  reading the converter provides - output and input voltage, charge current
  including the three measuring channels, board and both MOSFET temperatures,
  the CAN temperature sensor when one is connected, status byte and decoded
  bits, the pin 1 enable input, firmware and type as text - plus an energy
  counter that survives reboots and a high temperature alarm at 75/85 degrees.
  Optionally the temperatures can be shown as separate Venus devices, switched
  from the settings tree or from the Node-RED flow in extras/. The driver
  version is visible in the connection line on the device page, because gui-v2
  has no Package manager.

  Fixed in this version: the extra temperature devices were never created.
  VeDbusService attaches a handler to the root path "/", of which there is only
  one per D-Bus connection - each additional service now gets its own private
  connection.

v1.0 - v1.10
  development versions, in this order:
  v1.0   first release: voltages, current, temperatures, active state,
         registered as com.victronenergy.dcdc
  v1.1   /Mode mirrors the remote on/off input on pin 1, status changes logged
  v1.2   ReadMe: troubleshooting section
  v1.3   registers as com.victronenergy.alternator instead of dcdc, so the
         device appears on the overview page next to solar; an existing VRM
         instance is migrated
  v1.4   /DeviceOffReason 0x08 (remote connector) while pin 1 disables the unit
  v1.5   ReadMe: documented what the alternator device page does and does not show
  v1.6   all remaining converter readings published on the same device
  v1.7   /History/EnergyOut energy counter and /Alarms/HighTemperature
  v1.8   optional separate temperature devices, off by default
  v1.9   Node-RED flow in extras/ to switch them without a console
  v1.10  flow fixed: it writes the settings value, not the device path /Mode
